# Commit conventions

Use [Conventional Commits 1.0.0](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/) for every git commit in this repo. Do not use the older "Pass N:" subjects.

## Format

```
<type>[optional scope]: <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer(s)]
```

- Type is a lowercase noun, then optional `(scope)`, optional `!` for a breaking change, then `: ` and a description.
- Description is imperative, lowercase, no trailing period, about **why** in one short line.
- Body is optional; separate it from the subject with a blank line.
- Breaking changes use `type(scope)!:` and/or a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer.

## Types

- `feat` — user-facing capability
- `fix` — bug fix
- `docs` — documentation only
- `style` — formatting, no behaviour change
- `refactor` — behaviour-preserving restructure
- `perf` — performance
- `test` — tests
- `build` / `ci` — tooling and pipelines
- `chore` — maintenance that is none of the above

Scope is a short area noun when it helps (`themes`, `docs`, `landing`).

## Examples

```
feat(themes): add dashboard mail chat finances and crm previews
fix(docs): stop nested buttons in example previews
chore: ignore local next start logs
```
